{"title":"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems\">2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) #14</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) #17</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A rectangular sign that has dimensions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/2/672f1e9a6fd312a5370d8ee4eec24b1415fb5e0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b47ad4a8622dd1bce9d1e8bf85b6abc968c409e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" /> has a square advertisement painted on it. The border around the square is required to be at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/c/cbc3c32eeac2274b9465c49fd3b795c9a382679b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.5 \\text { m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> wide. The area of the largest square advertisement that can be painted on the sign is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/8/8c8fae11ffd2c1393f64a679de3d62900c971430.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 78 \\text{ m}^{2} \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 144 \\text{ m}^{2} \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 36 \\text{ m}^{2} \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 9 \\text{ m}^{2} \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 56.25 \\text{ m}^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"591\" height=\"21\" />  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We want to use the minimum border to get the largest square advertisement. Since the border is required to be at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/6/8f6d30b7ef123c5eed14e0ffb6cc8d53718342be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.5 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> wide, the minimum must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/c/cbc3c32eeac2274b9465c49fd3b795c9a382679b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.5 \\text { m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Removing the border, we can see that the dimensions are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/1/111c470c1ac39253c51774a20fe3a452a58e1be9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 - 1.5 \\times 2 = 9 - 3 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"186\" height=\"15\" /> m by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/a/d4a991ec0e330c646e1b3798d4d44d42b15a8a87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16 - 1.5 \\times 2 = 16 - 3 = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"213\" height=\"15\" /> m.\n</p><p>Because we cannot fit a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> m by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> m square on this, the maximum width of the square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> m. Thus, the largest area is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22e60f2f58989877bb57426e825cbdbe2a409f29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\text{ m} \\times 6 \\text{ m} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 36 \\text{ m}^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"197\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/w